// QA joints for the l6-accounts cross-module contract (11.3, Tier 1): the
// AUTH CHAIN provenance and the VIEWER THREADING matrix, both over a REAL
// cmd/mellifera server subprocess (the qaSerialStartServer harness —
// production middleware, Deps.Identity wired, viewerFor, the main.go
// OnProgress fan-out carrying the REAL watch detector) running the real
// scanner plugin subprocesses over REAL fixture libraries.
//
// TestAccountsAuthChainJoint is the PROVENANCE chain (spec: "Viewer
// resolution", "The write lands in the caller's own slot", "The detector
// fires beside the re-grab and is nil-safe"): a login-minted session resolves
// through identity.ResolveViewer into the store's visibleWhere on the wire
// (library A listed, library B ≡ 404), and a ≥90% progress PUT's completion
// detector inserts the watched row into THAT USER's ledger slot — asserted
// via a DIRECT read-only SQLite read of the server's dataDir/mellifera.db
// (never the wire). The slot read is what proves the 5.3 ctx-carried viewer
// survived every link (middleware → viewerFor → ResolveViewer → handler →
// ctx → detector → store write): a single dropped link degrades the
// detector's access.FromContext to the zero Viewer, whose UserID 0 lands the
// row in the slot-0 legacy row — so asserting the row EXISTS under the user's
// id AND is ABSENT from slot 0 pins every link at once. The plain
// (sub-threshold) write lands in the same user's slot the same way, and a
// hidden-library item refuses the write with 404 and no row anywhere.
//
// TestAccountsViewerThreadingMatrix is the THREADING matrix, minimum-tests
// style: ONE assertion engine, rows = (principal, surface, target, want),
// four principal kinds (env-admin token / user session / device BOUND to the
// grouped user via the real pairing + 9.3 bind surface / UNBOUND legacy
// device) × four read surfaces (library / item / series / progress) ×
// visible and hidden targets = 32 wire rows, plus ONE set block per
// principal proving the resolved SET (library list, listing emptiness,
// progress slots), plus a revoke/re-grant tail isolating the visibility
// CONJUNCT on an own-slot row. The outcomes come from the shipped deltas —
// hidden ≡ 404 on direct routes, 200-empty on listing slots (accounts
// "Grant-based default visibility"), the bind rides the user's grant union
// exactly ("Binding re-scopes the device"), the unbound legacy device sees
// all ("Legacy principals keep see-all"), and progress reads are own-slot
// AND visibility-conjunct ("Continue rows follow the viewer"). The matrix
// proves the WIRE agrees per principal kind; it does not re-derive the unit
// law.
//
// DELIBERATE NON-ASSERTIONS (honesty, not coverage gaps): a see-all viewer
// reading an item with rows in TWO slots (itA holds slot-0 and user rows) —
// which slot a see-all reader lands on is unspecified by any delta, so that
// row asserts only status 200 + item identity; the position discriminator
// lives on the own-slot rows (3) and on the single-slot itB (11). The full
// AC matrix (every endpoint class × every principal kind, including
// per-surface 200-empty law and write paths) is task 11.5's scope.
//
// HERMETIC: library roots anchor under t.TempDir(); the shikimori upstream
// is pinned to a local all-404 stub (no enrichment is asserted — derivation
// failures are log-and-skip and never touch scan status). Fixture identity
// constants are independent of every other qa fixture (no-coincidence
// discipline); every helper is qaAcct-prefixed to stay collision-free in
// package itest.
